  <section id="chart" aria-labelledby="chart-h">
    <h2 id="chart-h">Height Percentile Chart</h2>
    <figure class="tp-fig"><img src="/assets/images/height-percentile-chart.webp" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Height percentile chart for boys and girls from age 2 to adults, with median and percentile bands"><figcaption>Median and percentile bands for height from age 2 through adulthood, U.S. (NHANES 2015&ndash;2018).</figcaption></figure>
    <p>Boys and girls grow at nearly the same rate until about age 10. Girls then have their growth spurt earlier and stop growing around 15 to 16; boys keep growing until about 17 to 19, which opens the adult gap of about 13&nbsp;cm (5&nbsp;in).</p>
  </section>

